# The rig half of two records, on the release build with every knob at its
# default, every lap keeping both nodes' kernel logs (tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh
# laps exports PF_KEEP_KMSG=1, so a passing row copies kmsg_<node>_fromnode.gz
# into its evidence directory instead of deleting it).
#
#   D-MASTER-OWN-EX-RELEASE-GOES-STALE-RECORD-OUTLIVES-IT-PEER-GRANTS-REFUSED:
#   its verification rules (written before the H-MO2 patch) need the release
#   build to pass path_fenced_return and chk_clean on the rig with no
#   P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT naming the survivor.  The release chain's 10 window
#   laps passed their rows but kept no kernel log, so the double-grant count
#   was never read.
#
#   D-SURVIVOR-DEFERRED-PUBLISH-EX-CLAIM-FAILS-AFTER-60-REMASTER-RETRIES-AT-REJOIN:
#   seen once (window lap 7, three claims) in the only two minutes of kernel
#   ring that survived; its rate and what each failed inode does afterwards are
#   unmeasured.
#
# Build: the main tree's mxfs.ko, which must be the release build the chain
# verified (modinfo -F srcversion mxfs.ko = the chain's clean build); run from
# the main tree.  2/net/mesh/mpath on g2e (test17 test18), a group no release
# board or follow-on step uses once the chain's boards are done:
# path_fenced_return freezes and fences test18, thaws it, it unmounts and
# mounts again and reads test17's files; then chk_clean.  Every lap on a fresh
# prep, so each module load resets the capped probes and an absent line is not
# a spent cap.
#
# READING RULES (written before the first lap), per lap, from the row's
# kmsg_<node>_fromnode.gz scoped to the row's PF-MARK, graded with
# tools/dead_sender_ab_grade.py <row dir> plus the counts below:
#   D-MASTER-OWN
#     PASS (per lap)  path_fenced_return PASS, chk_clean verdict=CLEAN
#                     release=CLEAN errors=0, and double=s0 on both nodes (no
#                     P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT whose record ex= is the survivor).
#     Recorded, not graded: resync (P-TAUTH-OWN-REL-RESYNC per node), drops,
#     passes, stale_own, relex, and 'lock request failed after' per node.
#     FIXED AND VERIFIED on the rig side: every lap PASS.  Any lap with double
#     naming the survivor, or a peer request refused into 'lock request failed
#     after' on the inode the survivor held: REFUTED, a new hypothesis first.
#   D-SURVIVOR-DEFERRED-PUBLISH-EX-CLAIM-FAILS-...
#     RATE  laps with at least one 'deferred-publish CAW EX failed' on the
#           survivor, and the count per lap.
#     TRACE for each failed ino: every later line naming it on both nodes (a
#           later grant to the creator, a grant to the peer, a P-PUB re-list),
#           and whether the peer read it (the row's VERIFY covers the
#           survivor's manifest).
#     Recorded for the bar: any VERIFY bad or missing, any read of a failed
#     ino returning other bytes than the manifest's, any P-TAUTH-DOUBLE-GRANT
#     or double holder on a failed ino.
#     From the release candidate with pub_claim_retry and dl_capacity_park
#     (laps frke*): 'deferred-publish CAW EX failed' must be 0 on both nodes;
#     recorded per node: P-PUB-CLAIM-RETRY, P-PUB-CLAIM-RETRY-GRANTED,
#     P-CAP-PARK, P-CAP-PARK-EXPIRE.
#   D-TCP-LEDGER-PAGE-FULL-EDQUOT-SHUTS-DOWN-BOTH-NODES-AFTER-FENCED-PEER-REJOINS
#     PASS (per lap)  no 'rc=-122', no 'DLM inode lock unrecoverable', no
#                     shutdown on either node; recorded: P-TAUTH-PAGE-FULL per
#                     node (reach: a lap with page-full refusals and no -122
#                     is the fixed path working).
#   D-NETMESH-MPATH-REJOINED-NODE-HEARTBEAT-LOCKWAIT-STALL-DECLARED-DEAD
#     The survivor declares the frozen victim dead once (the row's fence).  A
#     second 'heartbeat expired' / 'lease expired/died' naming the victim's
#     REJOINED node id is a recurrence.  Laps frke* load the module with
#     stall_stacks=1 (MXFS_EXTRA_MODARGS, exported to the queue; it only
#     prints), so a P278-HB-STALL dumps the heartbeat task's stack; every
#     P278-HB-STALL and P-HB-SLOW on the rejoined node after its remount is
#     recorded with that stack.
#   From the release candidate with dl_capacity_reclaim, dl_capacity_nq_wouldblock,
#   reap_active_gate and lookup_poison_retire (laps frkf*):
#   D-TCP-CAPACITY-WAIT-NEVER-ENDS-HANGS-JOIN-FREEZE
#     PASS (per lap)  no hung task, no 'blocked for more than', the victim's
#                     remount completes; recorded per node: P-TAUTH-PAGE-FULL,
#                     P-CAP-RECLAIM, P-CAP-PARK, P-CAP-PARK-EXPIRE.
#   D-TCP-NOQUEUE-TRY-ON-FULL-LEDGER-PAGE-SPENDS-RETRY-BUDGET-CREATES-CRAWL
#     PASS (per lap)  no 'capacity=60' on either node; recorded per node:
#                     dl_capacity_nq_wouldblock_n read at the end of the lap.
#   D-FAILED-MOUNT-UNWIND-RACES-REAP-WORKER-FREES-AG-AND-HANGS
#     PASS (per lap)  no 'xg_ref', no 'Corruption detected', no mount left in
#                     D state; recorded: P-REAP-INACTIVE-DEFER lines.
#   D-ALLOC-WITNESS-PEER-MKDIR-ESTALE-ON-POISONED-CACHED-DIR-4CAW
#     PASS (per lap)  no 'Stale file handle' in any row output; recorded per
#                     node: P-LKUP-POISON-RETIRE, P-LKUP-POISON-RETURNED (0).
#   Any shutdown, BUG, Oops, hung task or chk_clean not CLEAN is attributed
#   from its own lines first.
#
# Bounds: tests/queues/dead_sender_drop_ab_netmesh_mpath.queue's lap, the same
# rows and prep (path_fenced_return 400 s + chk_clean 180 s + the chain's
# overhead outside the rows, measured 130-160 s = 730 s, plus prep_cluster
# 300 s) = 1030 s.
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf1 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf2 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf3 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf4 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf5 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf6 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf7 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf8 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf9 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf10 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf11 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
1030 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e frkf12 1 --prep --rows path_fenced_return,chk_clean
